course: dictionary
lesson: 5440
title: Lamppost in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the words around it. The sentence is its context, and the context leaves clues.
explain: Look at this: «Picture a lamppost in Dieppe with a poster: "Perdu : petit chat noir, yeux verts."» The poster is about a cat that is black and has green eyes. The first word, perdu, means lost, so this poster is looking for a lost cat. The clues in the sentence show you the meaning.
explain: In the first sentence, «They put their bins out at the same minute and look past each other like the other is a lamppost», the people are not talking about a real post. They ignore each other, as if the other one is not there. Always ask: does the meaning fit the sentence?
fact: A lamppost is a tall post in a street or park with a light at the top.
fact: The light on a lamppost comes on when it gets dark.
fact: Lampposts can also hold up signs, posters and bins.
fact: «Lamppost» is one lamppost, and «lampposts» is more than one.
fact: In stories, a lamppost may mark a meeting place.
exercise: What does a lamppost have at the top? | A flag that flies in the wind | A bird's nest | *A light that comes on when it gets dark | A bell that rings on the hour
exercise: «Picture a lamppost in Dieppe with a poster: "Perdu : petit chat noir, yeux verts."» What does perdu mean? | Black | *Lost | Sold | Found
exercise: «Jake and Kieran each swear they touched the lamppost first.» Find and copy the word that means a tall post with a light. | *lamppost | Jake | touched | first
test: Lily and Maddie argue about tig-backs. What is a tig-back? | *Tagging straight back the person who tagged you | Hiding behind a bin | Touching a lamppost first | Running away from a game of football
test: In the Dieppe poster, why is the lamppost a good place for it? | Cats like to sleep on posts | The poster is about a cat that is for sale | A lamppost can talk to cats | *Someone walking past at night could see the poster
exam: Which of these is NOT a use of a lamppost in the lessons? | *To grow flowers in the street | To hold a lost dog poster | To light a road at night | To mark a meeting place in a story
